    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe spec asked to define membership level 4 as requiring tenure of more than 365 days, while keeping a brand-new owner (zero tenure) capped at level 3.\n\nThe old `AssignMembershipLevel` simply did `Math.min(level, 3)` \u2014 level 4 was structurally unreachable and undefined. I replaced that hardcoded cap with an explicit tenure rule in `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/AssignMembershipLevel.java`:\n\n- The pre-tenure factors (base 1, +1 for email, +1 for `namesakeCount == 0`) are still capped at 3.\n- Level is promoted to 4 only when tenure (days from `registrationDate` to today) is **strictly greater than 365**.\n- A newly created owner's `registrationDate` is today (set by `ApplyRegistrationDate` and never later than the server date), so its tenure is 0 \u2192 it can never reach level 4. A new owner with an email and `namesakeCount` 0 lands at level 3, exactly as the `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` acceptance test asserts.\n\nTest results: `AcceptanceTest` passes and `mvnw test` reports `BUILD SUCCESS` (1 test, 0 failures \u2014 the acceptance suite is the only test class in the project).",
